# Thamba — local environment
# Copy to .env.local and fill in. Never commit .env.local or a real key.
# Next reads this file at startup, so restart `pnpm dev` after changing it.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Sign in (Privy)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Only the APP ID is needed. It is public by design and ships in the browser
# bundle, which is why it carries the NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix. The Privy app SECRET
# is for server-side calls (@privy-io/server-auth, verifying tokens) and this
# app makes none, so do not put a secret in here.
#
# Create an app at https://dashboard.privy.io. In its settings, allow
# http://localhost:3000 as a login domain, enable Email and Wallet as login
# methods, and turn on embedded wallets for users without one.
#
# Blank is a working state: the app falls back to a local demo sign-in sheet
# that mirrors the Privy flow. Real embedded wallets need a real id.
NEXT_PUBLIC_PRIVY_APP_ID=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Exchange data (services/api)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Base URL of the backend proxy. Every price, listing, application and policy
# on screen comes from it. Unset is a named state, not a crash: each screen
# shows an error card saying the server is not configured, with a Retry. The
# app never falls back to invented data.
#
#   Fixtures, no chain needed:   node dev/api-stub/server.mjs   -> port 8788
#   Real Sepolia:                cd ../services/api && npm start -> port 8788
#
# While pointed at the stub the app shows a "Demo data" strip on every screen.
# Point it at the real backend and the strip disappears on its own.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8788

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Chain
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sepolia RPC the browser uses for the few reads it makes directly rather than
# through the backend. Leave blank to use viem's default public endpoint, which
# is rate limited and fine for a demo. A dedicated endpoint is steadier.
NEXT_PUBLIC_RPC_URL=

# ENS names live on Ethereum mainnet, so resolving the signed-in address to a
# name is a mainnet read even though trading happens on Sepolia. One cached
# call per address. Blank uses viem's default public endpoint.
NEXT_PUBLIC_MAINNET_RPC_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. Issuer console
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The address that owns the listings, from contracts/deployments/<network>.json.
# The console compares the signed-in wallet against it and opens only for that
# wallet. Blank keeps the console open in DEMO MODE, which every console screen
# states on itself. There is no URL flag or local override that can grant it.
NEXT_PUBLIC_ISSUER_ADDRESS=
